        text: 'A Liander substation can carry 60 MW of offtake. Last year’s peak: 48 MW. Promised to new customers who are still building: 9 MW. Natural growth at existing customers: 2 MW a year, for the two years until the reinforcement is ready.\n\nFuture peak: 48 + 9 + 2 × 2 = 61 MW. That is above 60 MW: transport scarcity, even though the station seems to have 12 MW of room today. New applications go on the queue, and Liander starts a congestion management study.\n\nIf part of the 9 MW is never used, the picture changes; that is why use it or lose it matters.',
